  "concept_density": "high",
  "scope_boundary": "This chapter covers the Fundamental Rights enshrined in Part III of the Indian Constitution (Articles 12\u201335), including the definition of State, features of fundamental rights, detailed explanation of each right (equality, freedom, against exploitation, religion, cultural/educational, constitutional remedies), exceptions (Articles 31A, 31B, 31C), armed forces, martial law, and the historical abolition of the right to property. It does not cover Directive Principles of State Policy or Fundamental Duties in detail, nor does it provide a comprehensive treatment of foreign constitutions beyond comparative references. Amendments up to the 103rd Amendment Act (2019) are within scope.",
